    "1": {
      "note": "Cantonese cooking has three signature methods. <strong>zyu2</strong> (煮) is general cooking — boiling, simmering. <strong>caau2</strong> (炒) is stir-frying in a wok — high heat, quick motion. <strong>zing1</strong> (蒸) is steaming — used heavily for fish, dim sum, and Chinese desserts. The wok (<em>wok6</em>, 鑊) is the iconic Cantonese kitchen tool. Verb-object pattern: <em>caau2 coi3</em> (炒菜, stir-fried vegetables), <em>zing1 jyu2</em> (蒸魚, steamed fish).",
